From 416842028be33306c680f7dedf37a64cda3773e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:06:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 73/76] vgpu: answer the info encoder's queries

Component: exec info segments (all pathways).

From protocol 235 a macOS 27 guest asks two questions through its info
encoder instead of through child packets:
- heapTextureSizeAndAlignWithDescriptor: as record 0x1c3 (32-byte
  descriptor) or 0x1d5 (40-byte), in place of child 0x40;
- computePipelineStateInfo:info: as record 0x1c2, in place of child 0x3b.
Each names a reply buffer and offset. Nothing answered them, so the guest
read zero for every heap texture's size, and its kernel refused the
heaps with "invalid arguments"; it read zero threadgroup limits for every
compute pipeline and dispatched empty grids.

The heap query is answered by the same size-and-align computation as
0x40. The compute query writes the 28 bytes the guest copies into the
pipeline: maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup, threadExecutionWidth and
staticThreadgroupMemoryLength as u64s, from the values 0x3b answers.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237:
the guest's kernel logged 19 "invalid arguments" resource refusals in
one boot, and the desktop drew without its wallpaper. With both
queries answered (the compute reply buffers are pool buffers, read by
the previous patch) the wallpaper drew.

Verified: the reims-vgpu test suite passes; clippy unchanged.
Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
